# Copy to backend/.env for local dev (gitignored; `npm run dev` loads it).
# Leave these unset and GitHub sign-in is off: public repos still work.
#
# A dev GitHub App (see README "GitHub App"): callback URL
# http://localhost:5173/api/github/callback, webhooks off,
# Contents: read-only, Metadata: read-only.
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Path to the app's private key (.pem). Keep it outside the repo.
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=
TALON_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Google Drive connection (Connections panel). Leave unset and the card says
# "not set up". A Google Cloud project with the Drive API and Picker API on,
# an OAuth consent screen (External + Testing is fine for dev; add yourself
# as a test user), a Web OAuth client with redirect URI
# http://localhost:5173/api/connections/google_drive/callback, and an API
# key restricted to the Picker API. GOOGLE_PROJECT_NUMBER is the project
# NUMBER (digits, on the Cloud console dashboard; the client ID starts with
# it), not the project ID; it may be left empty.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_PICKER_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_PROJECT_NUMBER=
